    "body": "\r\n> Beyond that, shouldn't the tests already pass on Windows?\r\n\r\nNo, since the paths on Windows include the Drive letter (e.g. `C:\\Users\\User` → `[\"C\", \"\\Users\\User\"]`).\r\n\r\n> You are only adding a single path (so there is no platform-specific delimiter), there might be more issues here.\r\n\r\nI could add more test-cases. If the tests are running concurrently, this could introduce flaky tests.\r\n\r\n> I think it might better to append the env value instead of replacing and restoring it, maybe even adding it twice to test your upstream PR (thanks for fixing the upstream bug I introduced!).\r\n\r\nWouldn't that make the tests dependent on the outside environment?",
